  q-2026-10-02-001,2026-10-02-sample,Will spending two hours this week prototyping the smallest proof-agent experiment be higher-value than reading two more papers on it?,A recent open-source release makes small theorem-proving agents cheap to run locally.,prototype the experiment this week,keep reading first,news,82,90,70,65,88,exploit,Resolved true if a later note or repository shows the prototype ran and was judged more useful than the reading.,2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T08:00:00Z"
  q-2026-10-02-002,2026-10-02-sample,Should I stop project X before investing another ten hours in it?,The last three notes on X record no measurable progress.,stop X and write down why,continue X for ten more hours,notes,75,85,40,92,80,exploit,Resolved true if X is stopped within the horizon and no later note regrets it.,2026-11-01,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T08:00:00Z"
  q-2026-10-02-003,2026-10-02-sample,Am I continuing the site refactor because of sunk cost rather than expected future value?,Repository activity shows refactor commits but no new readers' features in a month.,freeze the refactor,finish the refactor,project,70,72,55,88,76,exploit,Unresolvable automatically unless a later note states the reason explicitly.,2026-12-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T08:00:00Z"
  q-2026-10-02-004,2026-10-02-sample,Will the result I rated 80% last session still look right after this month's new evidence?,Two later notes partly contradict it.,keep the belief,write a note revising it,calibration,60,45,35,70,66,exploit,Resolved by the next session's answer to the same latent variable.,next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T08:00:00Z"
  q-2026-10-02-005,2026-10-02-sample,Is a small immediate experiment better than more reading whenever my uncertainty is mainly empirical?,"",default to experiments first,keep deciding case by case,synthesis,66,58,62,50,70,explore,"Unresolved until several later records show experiments outperforming reading, or not.",2027-04-01,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T08:00:00Z"
